- Number of e-books read last two years: Higher number may indicate more academic reading, especially if combined with other factors.
- Number of printed books read last two years: Higher number suggests more academic reading.
- Favorite books for reading to spend leisure time: If leisure reading is mostly fiction or non-academic, less likely to read academic books most of the time.
- What is the change felt after reading books: "Increase Academic Performance" or "Increase Problem Solving Skill" may correlate with academic reading.
- Who influenced you to read books: "Teachers" or "Self-Decision" may correlate with academic reading.
- Which language books do you like to read: English may indicate academic reading more than others, but not strongly conclusive.
- Where do you read printed books: Library or Home may be more academic than During Travel.
- Do you read Newspaper: Not strongly related.
- The format used for reading books: Both or Printed might indicate more serious reading than only E-books.
- Frequency of reading books: "On everyday basis" or "A few times a week" correlates with reading academic books most of the time.

